      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 11
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You write about that things shouldn’t be behind a paywall, but you don’t say what features or why that specific feature shouldn’t be behind a paywall.\nI don’t see any of the current things you get as a required feature to have a good experience in VRC.\nIt’s all cosmetic or additional QOL on top of a already new and better system. \n100 fav avatars, you don’t need it and I would much rather you visit my world to get more of my avatars.\nUser icon; pure cosmetic to the nameplate. Not required at all.\nPhoto invites, yes it’s been requested but it’s not required to be able to send invites. Everyone gets custom text invites. \nNot trying to defend VRChat, but you’re not giving any examples to what features that are 100% required and shouldn’t be behind a paywall.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
