      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "People always say \"don't make people pay for X or Y\" but when asked what should be the incentive to subscribe at all, they generally don't have an answer.\nnot a VRC+ subscriber here, but from a business perspective I don't see why avatar/world upload doesn't require a VRC+ subscription. Hate me for that suggestion all you want, but asset upload is the one thing that results in increased running costs to VRC over the long run.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-20T05:45:05.008Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While I do think that monetization is important to fund development I feel it's equally important that all users benefit equally from feature updates.  A major strength of the VRChat platform is that it provides a fully featured experience to all users.  Creating a system that introduces a non-cosmetic user class distinction should be avoided.\nI'd prefer other avenues to monetize that do not introduce paywall friction to user growth and retention.  Funding development of a platform you appreciate and value should be it's own motivation and reward.",
